(Bug #27 regression: a nested If as the last action of a Repeat. Per
 LANGUAGE.md's termination rule 1, the If's own period closes the If
 (the innermost clause), not the Repeat — so a second period is needed to
 close the Repeat, and "after" then runs once, after the loop. Before the
 fix the Repeat never consumed a period at all; the If consumed its
 period and the second period was then swallowed by the Repeat's body
 loop, so "after" was absorbed as a per-iteration action and the program
 printed `x after x after`. Expected: x, x, after.)

Repeat 2 times, If true then, Print "x"..
Print "after".